    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d212">

                <pb facs="0399" n="309" sameAs="frus:frus1932v02/pg309"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">862.00/2821a: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Ambassador in
                        Germany (Sackett)</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1932-08-15T16:00:00-04:00">August 15, 1932—4
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>95. I hope you will find it possible to send more frequent and complete
                    telegraphic reports on the situation in Germany during these critical days. What
                    we want is not so much factual reporting as an analysis of the political
                    situation and the general trend of its probable development.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Castle</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
